"""Hypothetical decision exercises; no client outcomes or product promises."""
CASES={
'design-brief':'''An owner is preparing {name} and initially asks only for a more polished appearance. The project review identifies the actual required function: {function} The team writes an acceptance condition using the component test below and separates the visual preference from the property facts. An unresolved measurement or provider responsibility remains assigned before selection. The revised brief can now be used by the designer and local coordinator without either person having to guess what completion means.''',
'measurement-survey':'''The plan for {name} looks plausible in photographs, but one critical relationship has not been verified. The survey requirement is specific: {measure} The local reviewer records the actual condition, units and date, then connects the answer to the item or deliverable being approved. The purchase stays conditional until the relevant uncertainty is closed. The example demonstrates evidence control, not a universal dimension or a guarantee that an item will fit every similar property.''',
'product-specification':'''A proposed {name} appears close to the preferred concept, but the schedule lacks an exact supported identifier or scope. The useful selection question is: {selection} The purchaser requests the missing document, records the accepted version and gives the receiver enough information to recognize a mismatch. A later alternative must be compared with that record rather than approved from appearance alone. The result is a traceable decision; no particular brand or advertised label is assumed to be universally suitable.''',
'sample-and-use-trial':'''The owner is uncertain about an aspect of {name}. The team defines an ordinary-use trial rather than a general product challenge: {test} It records the exact setup, participant, permitted method and observed result. A finding about fit or clarity is kept separate from a preference and from a technical issue requiring professional review. If the outcome is accepted, its limits remain on the record so a future purchaser does not mistake a narrow observation for a promise about all use.''',
'landed-cost-budget':'''A hypothetical {name} purchase is initially compared using only its product or service price. The owner lists the actual scope needed to obtain the accepted result and requests missing charges rather than entering assumed free work. The evidence package also needs to remain traceable: {records} The entered total is reviewed alongside unresolved allowances, payment timing and accepted quantities. This illustrates cost organization, not market pricing, tax treatment or a forecast that furnishing expenditure will produce a particular rental return.''',
'quote-scope-review':'''Two proposals for {name} use similar headline language, but the responsible tasks are not yet aligned. The owner sends the same function to both: {function} Each provider is asked to identify the deliverable, implementation and acceptance responsibilities. An unanswered task remains open and any missing cost is requested before comparing the complete quoted result. Either provider may still suit the property; the exercise makes the decision specific instead of declaring a winner from an incomplete number.''',
'receiving-and-condition-check':'''A {name} order or deliverable arrives, but the original acceptance question is not yet closed. The receiver compares the exact identifier and scope, retaining the relevant evidence: {records} A mismatch is recorded separately from accepted inventory and assigned through the actual provider process. Installation or implementation does not silently proceed on the assumption that arrival proves correctness. The exception closes only after the corrected result and any quantity or credit record reconcile.''',
'installation-handoff':'''The team is ready to implement {name}, but the installer has received an earlier version of the plan. The owner supplies the current site and product information and asks the responsible provider to confirm the task requirements. The agreed scope must preserve the component's actual role: {function} Any specialist question remains with the appropriate professional. The handoff ends with required completion evidence and a visible punch list rather than assuming every task was included in a broad installation label.''',
'guest-use-commissioning':'''The installed {name} is visually complete. An unfamiliar reviewer now follows the ordinary task under recorded conditions: {test} The team separates confusing information, a layout interference and a possible product or technical defect. It chooses a remedy appropriate to the observed issue, then repeats the affected check. This supports a particular accepted arrangement without claiming universal suitability, technical certification or a causal link to later booking performance.''',
'turnover-reset':'''The local team is asked to restore {name} after ordinary use. The documented reset requirement is: {reset} A repeated search or movement problem is recorded with its context. The owner compares a storage or instruction change with a product change and trials a defined remedy. The accepted record includes the current arrangement and exception owner. One trial is not extrapolated into guaranteed annual labor savings or a performance judgment about the cleaner.''',
'care-and-maintenance':'''The selected {name} has a general marketing description, but the local team needs an exact care method. The relevant component requirement is: {reset} The owner obtains the appropriate instructions, reviews equipment and service capacity, and keeps unsupported steps open. A permitted trial can clarify the process, while technical or persistent condition concerns receive qualified review. The care card is updated if the product or revision changes instead of assuming the first approval applies indefinitely.''',
'spares-and-replacement-support':'''The owner wants backup support for {name} but has not confirmed compatibility. The component record provides the starting evidence: {records} The provider is asked which parts, files or services can actually remedy an interruption. Stock or source information is labeled and assigned a location, with an authorized handling process. The plan is reviewed after real use, and obsolete compatibility assumptions are removed. A full-looking closet is not treated as proof of useful replacement capacity.''',
'fault-observation':'''A local reviewer reports a condition issue involving {name}. The team describes what is observed and considers this known failure mode: {failure} It does not assume that the observation proves the cause. The issue is assigned to the provider or qualified professional able to review it, with original identifiers and evidence. Closure requires the accepted remedy and relevant recheck, followed by updates to inventory or instructions if the installed result changes.''',
'substitution-approval':'''A replacement for {name} is offered with an attractive price or availability. The owner returns to the actual selection requirement: {selection} Exact dimensions, scope, care, access and compatible support are reviewed where relevant. The decision includes the complete quoted cost change and the records that must be updated. Approval occurs before commitment. The accepted substitution is checked after delivery or implementation rather than assumed correct from a similar photograph or product name.''',
'phased-refresh':'''The owner wants to improve {name} while coordinating the wider property. The phase starts from the actual function: {function} The team maps approval, preparation, receiving, implementation and acceptance dependencies. Temporary availability and storage effects are communicated to the operating owner. The phase is accepted only when the relevant checks and remaining limitations are clear. Actual work, purchases and chronology are retained for later review without assigning tax treatment from the word refresh.''',
'photo-and-listing-accuracy':'''A proposed image of {name} looks effective, but the listing owner checks it against the accepted function: {function} Temporary items and unresolved conditions are identified before publication. The selected views explain the real configuration rather than imply an unsupported feature. Image rights, file dates and channels are recorded. After a meaningful change, the register identifies what needs updating so an old attractive photograph does not become inaccurate guest information.''',
'warranty-and-provider-support':'''A support question arises for {name}. The owner collects the actual evidence package: {records} The exact agreement is reviewed for relevant scope, use conditions, exclusions and reporting steps. A hoped-for remedy remains separate from a confirmed action or credit. Any replacement or corrected deliverable is checked before closure and downstream records are updated. The example organizes provider communication without declaring a legal entitlement from a general warranty headline.''',
'financial-record-handoff':'''The financial reviewer asks what was actually purchased or performed for {name}. The owner provides the relevant documents and installed evidence: {records} Bundled descriptions, credits, later changes and chronology are reconciled or marked as questions. No classification or allocation percentage is invented to fill a missing field. The professional reviewer determines what additional evidence and treatment are appropriate. The outcome is a traceable record package, not a guaranteed deduction or savings estimate.''',
'operating-review':'''Repeated observations suggest a question about {name}. The owner reviews this component-specific failure mode without assuming it explains every event: {failure} The issue is classified and compared with the original function and current reset. A narrow remedy is trialed with documented conditions and full costs. If accepted, the inventory, care and guest information are revised. A later commercial change is not automatically attributed to the design intervention.''',
}
assert len(CASES)==19
